TITLE:: DrumProgrammer
SUMMARY:: Drum-machine step grid with looping playback.
CATEGORIES:: GUI>Views
RELATED:: Classes/AmpCommand, Classes/CommandPrompt, Classes/DrumStep, Classes/EnhancedButton, Classes/GuiPalette, Classes/PlayableNote, Classes/SCViewHolder, Classes/ScrollView, Classes/SequencePlayer, Classes/StaticText, Classes/SwitchCommand, Classes/View, Classes/Window

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::DrumProgrammer:: is a LINK::Classes/SCViewHolder:: that shows a grid of step squares on a LINK::Classes/GuiPalette:: colour1 background. Sound names and MIDI note numbers are held in a class LINK::Classes/Dictionary:: for now. It opens with one row of 16 squares for each sound, ordered by MIDI note number ascending from top to bottom: Kick 2 (35), Kick 1 (36), Rim (37), Snare (38), Clap (39), Tom 1 (41), Closed hi-hat (42), Tom 2 (43), Open hi-hat (46), Cymbal (49), Ride (51), Cowbell (56). Each row has its sound name in a LINK::Classes/StaticText:: on the left. That label column is as wide as the longest name. Click a sound name to select that row; click it again to clear the selection, or click another name to move it. The selected row's squares are outlined with LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-extreme2::, unless that square is also in the column currently playing. A LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt:: along the top offers LINK::Classes/AmpCommand:: and LINK::Classes/SwitchCommand::. LINK::Classes/AmpCommand:: uses the selected row's hits. LINK::Classes/SwitchCommand:: uses every LINK::Classes/DrumStep:: in that row, including empty squares. The grid sits in a LINK::Classes/ScrollView:: above the button strip, which stays put, and a scrollbar appears only when the grid is larger than that area.

Each square is a LINK::Classes/DrumStep::. Clicking an empty square adds a hit and colours the square with colour3. Clicking it again removes the hit and restores colour5. Each hit is a LINK::Classes/PlayableNote:: with velocity 100. The column is a sixteenth note (start time CODE::columnIndex * 0.25:: beats) and the note lasts CODE::0.0625:: beats. MIDI is sent on channel 10. CODE::switch 1 0 0 0:: sets hit, rest, rest, rest, and then repeats, including columns that were empty. An existing hit keeps its velocity.

A strip along the bottom holds the controls. Play starts the LINK::Classes/SequencePlayer:: from beat 0. The loop runs to the last step and then wraps. A second Play while already playing does nothing. While playing, the squares in the current column are outlined with LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-extreme2::, unless that square is also in the selected row. Stop ends playback and clears that outline. Add step appends a column on the right of every row and lengthens the loop. If that column was removed earlier, its hits are shown again and play once the loop includes them. Remove step removes the rightmost column and is disabled when there are no steps. Hits in a removed column are kept. Removing the last step also stops playback. Add drum sound and Remove drum sound are hidden. Removing a row drops the hits for that drum sound.

It does not create a window. Place an instance in a LINK::Classes/Window:: layout to show it.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates an instance of TELETYPE::DrumProgrammer::.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::DrumProgrammer:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

PRIVATE:: init, initClass, prAddDrumSound, prAddNote, prAddStep, prAllNotesInRow, prAppendDrumSound, prClearColumnHighlight, prClearRowSelection, prDropNotesForNoteNumber, prFindNote, prHighlightColumn, prInstallRow, prMakeButton, prMakeLabel, prMakeRow, prMakeStep, prNoteStartTime, prPlay, prRefreshRemoveButtons, prRemoveDrumSound, prRemoveNote, prRemoveStep, prSelectRow, prSelectedNotes, prSetButtonEnabled, prSortedDrumSoundNames, prStop, prSyncRowBackground, prSyncRowBorders, prSyncSequence, prSyncSquareBorder, prUpdateLoopEnd

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
(
var window = Window("Window", Rect(100, 100, 1000, 800));
window.layout = VLayout(DrumProgrammer()).margins_(0);
window.front;
)
::
